rent epic AC (per the recorded feasibility recommendation) so the leaf's `check-access`-only Cloud mutation is a faithful subset rather than a redefinition claimed as full AC satisfaction.","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent AC: 'A Live External Integration workflow runs GREEN ... fully exercising this epic's coordinator, create/binding-lifecycle, commit-unknown recovery, and endpoint/provider fuse functionality end-to-end against BOTH a live Jira Cloud instance and a live Jira Data Center instance'.","Leaf claim: 'This makes the Live External Integration workflow genuinely exercise live Cloud mutation, satisfying the epic's Cloud AC with real transport + credentials.'","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py L149-183: run_access_check calls client.create_issue / _direct_rest_put_raw / set_issue_property / search_issues directly — it does not invoke the coordinator, ticket_planner, apply_outbound create-and-bind, pass_fuse, or commit-unknown recovery named in the epic's file_impact/ACs.","By contrast tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py drives the real outbound create-and-bind pass (the coordinator path) live.","Parent's recorded feasibility comment recommends read-only Cloud + fakes for fuse/commit-unknown, but this was 'surfaced to operator'; the AC text was not amended and the epic is still in_progress — so the leaf's completion claim runs against the parent AC as written."],"finding":"The leaf claims its `rebar bridge check-access` Cloud lane 'satisfies the epic's Cloud AC', but the epic's REQUIRED Cloud AC demands the live-Cloud lane exercise THIS EPIC'S coordinator / create-binding-lifecycle / commit-unknown recovery / endpoint-provider fuse end-to-end (as the DC lane does), whereas `check-access` (access_check.run_access_check) is a standalone probe that bypasses the coordinator entirely.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1867bd981eaeea0e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan 'Outcome' and 'Context/Problem'; epic RP-03 (4217-d1d6) final Cloud Acceptance Criterion","norm_id":"nad1115e4b70b541e","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Epic-close gate: this leaf's GREEN Cloud lane is treated as fulfilling the Cloud AC, but the live-Cloud coordinator/create-binding path is never exercised, leaving the epic's REQUIRED gate only partially met.","A reviewer verifying the Cloud AC finds the coordinator create/binding-lifecycle exercised only against DC, not Cloud."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Pin the teardown step's exact acli command surface (e.g. `acli jira workitem search --jql 'labels ~ \"rebar-id:\"' --json` to list, then `acli jira workitem delete --key <k> --yes` to delete non-interactively), verified against the pinned ACLI_VERSION's `--help`, so the failure/cancel sweep cannot hang on a confirmation prompt or silently match nothing.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3044,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'runs a label-sweep teardown backstop that deletes any leaked `rebar-id:` probe issue' and 'lists+deletes leftover `labels ~ \"rebar-id:\"` issues' — no acli command/flags named.","Repo established surface: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_outbound_differ_live_comment_fetch.py references `acli jira workitem search --jql ... --paginate --json`; the delete verb is `acli jira workitem delete`.","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py:765: '`acli jira workitem delete` waits on stdin for confirmation' — a non-interactive CI step needs an explicit confirmation flag (e.g. --yes) or it hangs/fails.","Flag-level empiricism: the other Cloud lanes in external-integration.yml pin exact acli invocations; this teardown does not."],"finding":"The failure/cancel label-sweep teardown step asserts an acli list+delete-by-JQL capability but does not name the acli subcommand or its flags, and the repo's established delete surface requires non-interactive confirmation.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7b79cf45497597ec","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Outcome 2(c) / Plan step 2 — the `if: failure() || cancelled()` teardown that 'lists+deletes leftover `labels ~ \"rebar-id:\"` issues'","norm_id":"nd0deaf9b703cd363","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A probe issue leaks after a mid-run cancel; the teardown step runs `acli jira workitem delete` interactively, blocks on the stdin confirmation prompt, and the CI step hangs until timeout — leaving the leak uncleaned.","The list command flags (--jql / --json / --paginate) are guessed at implementation time and mismatch the pinned acli version, so the sweep matches nothing and silently reports success."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Name the acli subcommands and flags in the plan, matching the repo's established `acli jira workitem search --jql ... --json` list path and `acli jira workitem delete` with an explicit non-interactive confirmation flag (per acli.py's stdin-confirmation note), and state that they were confirmed against the pinned acli version's --help.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: robust"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the concrete default JQL-retry values (attempt count, base sleep seconds, backoff cap) and the target Cloud index-lag magnitude they must cover, so the default is a decision rather than 'covers observed REB lag'.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.325,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Raise the default budget to cover observed REB lag'","'a safe default that covers observed REB lag'","'sleeps with exponential backoff (base * 2**attempt, capped)' — the cap value is unspecified","Signal (2): implicit acceptance criteria — the numeric target for 'observed REB lag' (e.g. seconds of index-consistency delay to tolerate) is not quantified"],"finding":"The concrete new default values for the JQL retry budget (attempt count, base sleep, and the backoff cap) are not stated — the plan defers them to 'a default that covers observed REB lag', which is a design number left to the executor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2a4f5eac1c9880df","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Outcome #1 / Plan #1 / AC line 1","norm_id":"n2a4c05beb20587e0","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must pick retry count / base sleep / cap without a stated target and may choose a budget that still under-covers real Cloud lag, re-introducing the flake"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Quote the observed REB index-lag figure and pin defaults, e.g. JIRA_PROBE_JQL_RETRIES default N, JIRA_PROBE_JQL_SLEEP default Ss, backoff cap Cs, cumulative worst-case >= observed lag; have the unit test assert PASS at that worst-case boundary.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Pin the concrete default backoff schedule: state the new default retry count, the base sleep, the per-attempt cap value, and the resulting worst-case total wait, and confirm it exceeds observed REB index lag and fits the job's timeout.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.325,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'sleeps with exponential backoff (`base * 2**attempt`, capped) between attempts' — 'capped' has no value","Plan: 'Raise the default budget to cover observed REB lag' — the observed lag magnitude and the new default count/total-wall-time are not stated","Job has timeout-minutes ceilings (jira-cloud-s3-rehearsal uses 45m); an uncapped/underspecified backoff could interact with the new job's timeout"],"finding":"The exponential-backoff formula is specified as `base * 2**attempt, capped` but the cap value (and the resulting total worst-case budget) is left unspecified, so 'a safe default that covers observed REB lag' is not pinned to a concrete schedule the implementer can reproduce or the CI timeout can accommodate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f59e198a4a9d8b2f1","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 / AC line 1 ('exponential backoff ... with a safe default that covers observed REB lag')","norm_id":"neaaa060dbebb3a31","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer picks a per-attempt cap and retry count whose worst-case total under-covers real Cloud lag, reintroducing the flake","The unit test's asserted backoff schedule and the actual default diverge because the cap/count were never pinned"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Scope the failure/cancel label-sweep teardown to the CURRENT run's uniquely-labeled probe issue (e.g. match the run-specific `rebar-id:` label, not the shared prefix) so concurrent/overlapping probe runs don't delete each other's in-flight issues.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'on failure/cancel runs a label-sweep teardown backstop that deletes any leaked `rebar-id:` probe issue'","Plan step 2: 'lists+deletes leftover `labels ~ \"rebar-id:\"` issues'","The probe issue is 'uniquely-labeled' per run, but the sweep matches the shared `rebar-id:` prefix, not the run's unique label"],"finding":"The failure/cancel teardown backstop deletes ALL issues matching `labels ~ \"rebar-id:\"`, but concurrent probe runs (e.g. two dispatched Live External Integration runs, or a local `check-access` overlapping a CI run) each create their own uniquely-labeled probe issue under the same `rebar-id:` label prefix. A failing run's sweep would then delete another run's in-flight probe issue, causing that other run to fail mid-probe (its create/read target vanishes).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc1e22c0a1c93b32b","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 2 / AC: 'failure/cancel label-sweep teardown backstop that deletes any leaked `rebar-id:` probe issue'","norm_id":"n916cf7213f487b03","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two Live External Integration runs dispatched close together (or a re-run overlapping a prior run): run A fails, its sweep deletes run B's still-in-flight probe issue, so run B's property-read/JQL steps fail on a now-missing issue — a false failure attributed to the wrong run."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Have the probe emit its unique label into a job output/env and have the sweep filter on that exact per-run label; reserve any broad `rebar-id:` prefix sweep for an explicitly-scheduled janitor that only removes issues older than a safety window.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Evaluate Atlassian's documented read-after-write remedy — the `reconcileIssues` parameter on POST /rest/api/3/search/jql (which the codebase already POSTs to via _direct_rest_post_json in acli_graph.py) — as an alternative or complement to the backoff/retry-budget workaround, and either adopt it or record why it is inapplicable to the probe's search path (e.g. the ACLI `jira workitem search` CLI in acli.py cannot pass reconcileIssues).","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan Context: 'the retry budget is a fixed JQL_RETRY_COUNT=6 x JQL_RETRY_SLEEP=5s with no backoff, which is shorter than Jira Cloud's search-index eventual-consistency lag, so the step flakes no_results_after_retry'","Retrieved Atlassian docs (developer.atlassian.com/cloud/jira/platform/search-and-reconcile/): 'The API doesn't provide read-after-write consistency by default... subsequent search operations using the API without the reconcileIssues parameter may return stale or outdated data instead of the most recent updates for some time.'","Retrieved (NodePit mirror of Atlassian search/jql op): 'If you need read-after-write consistency, you can utilize the reconcileIssues parameter to ensure stronger consistency assurances.'","Codebase already uses the endpoint that accepts reconcileIssues: acli_graph.py POSTs to /rest/api/3/search/jql via _direct_rest_post_json (get_parent_map, get_comment_map, get_issuelinks_map)","The plan text never mentions reconcileIssues or any consistency parameter — the remedy is pure polling-budget tuning"],"finding":"The plan root-causes the STEP_JQL_SEARCH flake as inherent Jira Cloud search-index eventual-consistency lag and prescribes a polling workaround (exponential backoff + larger retry budget) without considering Atlassian's documented first-class read-after-write remedy: the `reconcileIssues` parameter on the enhanced JQL search endpoint (POST /rest/api/3/search/jql), which the codebase already POSTs to elsewhere.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f366f6ca51d563466","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Outcome item 1 / Plan step 1 / Context-Problem paragraph ('shorter than Jira Cloud's search-index eventual-consistency lag')","norm_id":"n3fd22c4525308ba5","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Cloud index lag exceeds even the raised backoff budget, re-flaking the probe that reconcileIssues would have made deterministic","Reviewer/maintainer later asks why a documented vendor consistency parameter was passed over in favour of a longer poll"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In Outcome/Plan step 1, add a prior-art note: cite that Jira Cloud's enhanced JQL endpoint offers reconcileIssues for read-after-write consistency; if the probe switches its STEP_JQL_SEARCH visibility check to the REST /rest/api/3/search/jql path with reconcileIssues=[issueKey], the flake is eliminated deterministically. If the probe must keep using the ACLI CLI search (which does not expose reconcileIssues), state that explicitly and keep backoff as the fallback with that justification recorded.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacke